.33Z","fill":"#231f20"},{"d":"M293.76 376.41H306.39V376.91H293.76Z","fill":"#231f20"},{"d":"M333.98 449.03H346.61V449.53H333.98Z","fill":"#231f20"}],"figs":[]}],"content":[{"type":"text","tex":"B MODELLING (QUESTIONS 6 TO 9)"},{"type":"text","tex":"HIGH RIVER FLOW (30 marks)"},{"type":"text","tex":"You are advised to spend no more than 50 minutes on this part."},{"type":"text","tex":"This task looks at estimating the probability of high river flows."},{"type":"text","tex":"Planners need to estimate the probability of extreme events such as high river flow. To do this they use the return period, \\(R\\) years. This is an estimate of the number of years before they expect another high river flow."},{"type":"text","tex":"A model for \\(R\\) is"},{"type":"text","tex":"\\(R = \\frac{n+1}{h}\\)"},{"type":"text","tex":"where \\(n\\) is the number of years for which there are river flow results, \\(h\\) is the number of times that high river flow occurs during the \\(n\\) years."},{"type":"text","tex":"The probability of high river flow occurring in any year is \\(\\frac{1}{R}\\) ."},{"type":"text","tex":"\\(\\frac{Example}{On 3}\\) occasions during a period of 65 years, a river flow was greater than 4000 cubic metres per second \\((m^{3}\\) /s)."},{"type":"text","tex":"So, the return period for a water flow greater than \\(4000m^{3}\\) /s is"},{"type":"text","tex":"\\(R = \\frac{65+1}{3} = \\frac{66}{3}\\)"},{"type":"text","tex":"\\(= 22\\) years."},{"type":"text","tex":"This is not very likely in a year, but very likely in the lifetime of a bridge designed to last for 100 years."},{"type":"text","tex":"The probability of a river flow greater than \\(4000m^{3}\\) /s in any year is \\(\\frac{1}{22}\\) ."}],"tex_check":"ok"}]}